# Licensing, provenance and clean room

Full detail: `docs/notepads/Licensing_and_Provenance.md` and spec sections 2 and 4.3.

## Header for every original source file (C++, PowerShell, schemas with comments)

```cpp
// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
// SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 The APP Authors
```

Use the comment syntax of the file type (`#` for PowerShell and YAML). JSON files without comment support are exempt.

## Reusing outside code

- Fresh implementation is the default. Reuse open-source code only when it is GPL-3.0-compatible (spec 4.3) and saves substantial effort on a hard problem.
- **Never** copy GPL-2.0-only code, proprietary code, "source-available" code, code with no licence, or anything from SOLIDWORKS, Altium or other proprietary CAD (code, SDK headers, docs, icons, sample files, UI layouts).
- When you reuse code, in the same change:
  1. keep the original copyright and licence lines at the top of the file, then add `SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 The APP Authors` for your modifications;
  2. put verbatim third-party files under `third_party/<project>/`; adapted code may live in `src/` but is marked with `// Adapted from <project> <url> @ <commit>`;
  3. add a row to `docs/provenance.md`: project, URL, version/commit, original path, licence, destination files, what was changed;
  4. update `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`.
- `scripts/check-spdx.ps1` fails on missing headers or on third-party markers without a provenance entry.

## Data

- Seed data (materials, fasteners, profiles, hole tables, footprint parameters) comes from public factual sources. Record each source in `docs/data-sources.md`. Never reproduce paid standards documents verbatim.
- Do not name UI features with vendor trademarks; use generic engineering terms.
